Pass provider 'anthropic' to the history formatter for Anthropic runs

formatAgentMessages only takes its Anthropic-specific paths (server tool
result pairing, duplicate tool_call de-dupe, inline tool_use) when it is given
options.provider, which LibreChat never passed. Pass it when any reachable agent
is Anthropic (including custom endpoints with provider: anthropic). The
memory-agent formatting call stays provider-less. Non-Anthropic agents in the
same run get the shared history projected back to their own shape by
@librechat/agents (pkg-patches 006).

